{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Pe9SY6GhX9HBR773RmBchK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## FINDINGS LEDGER\n- Current hypothesis: For flag options sharing a name, each option's `default` is set independently. When click resolves a value for the unset CLI run, it iterates options and the one with `default=True` should win (mapping to `flag_value`). In 8.3.0, UNSET normalization may overwrite that. Inspect `consume_value` and per-option default logic.\n- Evidence found: core.py:2771-2772 — `if self.default is True and self.flag_value is not UNSET: self.default = self.flag_value`. That handles per-option. But each option is processed independently in `consume_value`, so defaults of `--red`/`--blue` (UNSET → None?) may overwrite the green default depending on order.\n- Affected files: test-repos/click/src/click/core.py (around 2270-2335, 2750-2790)\n- Confidence: 0.30\n- Next action: Read core.py lines 2260-2340 (consume_value) and 2750-2800 (Option init).\n- Reason for next action: Determine how option defaults overwrite each other for shared name."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2165,"cache_read_input_tokens":21425,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2165},"output_tokens":41,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6096e1fa-1746-4526-90b9-751fb91b4297","uuid":"a0405353-c58b-4bb7-8844-f38bd8ce1ca2"}
